@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+## Context
+
+`merge` is used both to apply a patch and, wrongly, to copy values.
+
+## Decisions
+
+Add a `clone` helper that deep-copies JSON values (own enumerable keys, via `setMember` for safe keys). Use it for target members and patch array items. Patch objects applied onto a missing target member still go through `merge`, so nulls there are dropped as RFC 7386 requires.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-merge-patch-null-copy/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-merge-patch-null-copy/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0e3dc77bffd7e80b179486768032056265545fef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-merge-patch-null-copy/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Why
+
+`applyMergePatch` copies target members and patch arrays by calling `merge(undefined, value)`, which treats them as patches and strips `null` members from nested objects. Stored data is silently lost, contrary to RFC 7386 and the spec.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Target members that the patch does not touch are copied verbatim, nested `null` members included.
+- Arrays in the patch are copied verbatim (deep copy), nested `null` members included.
+- Tests cover both cases.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-merge-patch`: make explicit that untouched target content and arrays keep their `null` members.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/json-merge-patch.ts` and `test/json-merge-patch.test.ts`.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-merge-patch-null-copy/specs/json-merge-patch/spec.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-fix-merge-patch-null-copy/specs/json-merge-patch/spec.md
new file mode 100644
